"},{"type":"text","text":"All 18 tests pass. Now let me analyze the implementation for refactoring.\n\n## Refactoring Analysis\n\n### Step 1: Naming Evaluation (FIRST PRIORITY)\n\n- `runScenario` — accurately describes processing a scenario's steps. ✓\n- `quotePremium` — clearly computes a premium quote. ✓\n- `loyaltyDiscountFor` — clear. ✓\n- `surchargeFor` — clear higher-order helper. ✓\n\nNames are strong. No renaming needed.\n\n### Step 2: Identify Improvement (Rule 3 — No Duplication)\n\nI see **conceptual duplication**: `loyaltyDiscountFor` and the inline `followUpDiscount` both express \"a percentage of `basePremium`, applied only when a condition holds.\" The loyalty case is wrapped in a named helper; the follow-up case is an inline ternary. These are the same concept represented two different ways.\n\n### Step 3: APP Mass — `quotePremium` discount portion (before)\n\n```\nloyaltyDiscountFor: params(basePremium, years)=2 bindings, conditional=4, invocation(*)... \n```\n\nLet me measure the two discount concepts:\n\n**Before:**\n- `loyaltyDiscountFor`: bindings 2, invocation `*` (2), conditional `?:` (4), constants 0, binding refs (basePremium, LOYALTY_RATE) → ~ 2 + 2 + 4 + 2 = 10\n- inline `followUpDiscount = isFollowUp ? basePremium * FOLLOW_UP_RATE : 0`: assignment(6) + conditional(4) + invocation(2) + bindings(2) + constant(1) = 15\n- **Discount concept total: ~25**\n\nLet me unify both under a single conditional-percentage helper."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01QVBK5PgRYapTfxQuFWC9Bq","name":"edit","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_15-24-24_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_opus-4-8-5/src/claim-office.ts","edits":[{"oldText":"const loyaltyDiscountFor = (basePremium: number, yearsWithMHPCO: number): number =>\n  yearsWithMHPCO >= LOYALTY_THRESHOLD_YEARS ? basePremium * LOYALTY_RATE : 0;","newText":"const percentageWhen = (base: number, rate: number, applies: boolean): number =>\n  applies ? base * rate : 0;\n\nconst isLoyalCustomer = (yearsWithMHPCO: number): boolean =>\n  yearsWithMHPCO >= LOYALTY_THRESHOLD_YEARS;"},{"oldText":"  const loyaltyDiscount = loyaltyDiscountFor(basePremium, yearsWithMHPCO);\n  const followUpDiscount = isFollowUp ? basePremium * FOLLOW_UP_RATE : 0;","newText":"  const loyaltyDiscount = percentageWhen(basePremium, LOYALTY_RATE, isLoyalCustomer(yearsWithMHPCO));\n  const followUpDiscount = percentageWhen(basePremium, FOLLOW_UP_RATE, isFollowUp);"}]}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-opus-4-8@eu","usage":{"input":6305,"output":1738,"cacheRead":9935,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":17978,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784907521565,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-97657547-7e23-4214-825f-ef91f4b4a3d6","responseModel":"claude-opus-4-8"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01QVBK5PgRYapTfxQuFWC9Bq","toolName":"edit","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully replaced 2 block(s) in /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_15-24-24_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_opus-4-8-5/src/claim-office.ts."}],"details":{"diff":"     ...\n  72 \n  73 const isHighEnchantment = (item: Item): boolean =>\n  74   (item.enchantment ?? 0) >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD;\n  75 \n- 76 const loyaltyDiscountFor = (basePremium: number, yearsWithMHPCO: number): number =>\n- 77   yearsWithMHPCO >= LOYALTY_THRESHOLD_YEARS ? basePremium * LOYALTY_RATE : 0;\n+ 76 const percentageWhen = (base: number, rate: number, applies: boolean): number =>\n+ 77   applies ? base * rate : 0;\n  78 \n+ 79 const isLoyalCustomer = (yearsWithMHPCO: number): boolean =>\n+ 80   yearsWithMHPCO >= LOYALTY_THRESHOLD_YEARS;\n+ 81 \n  79 const quotePremium = (items: Item[], yearsWithMHPCO: number, isFollowUp: boolean): number => {\n  80   const mainItems = items.filter((item) => !isComponent(item));\n  81   const components = items.fil