:0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784907629869,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-ae69b0fd-3433-421b-ab02-19385a64e475","responseModel":"claude-opus-4-8"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01TxDDHKt9QhL6Yu4T1AC6PJ","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"      Tests  21 passed | 20 todo (41)\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784907632564},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Green Phase Complete: 21 passing."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01KMNJFRut4x6NRQMycoweQi","name":"subagent","arguments":{"agent":"refactor","agentScope":"both","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 21\nRecent Green phase: Added claim processing. INSURANCE_VALUES map, Policy tracking (items + remainingCap = 2x insurance sum), processClaim computes payout per damage (amount - 100 deductible, floored, capped by remainingCap) and decrements remainingCap. runScenario now handles both quote and claim steps, storing policies by step index.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. Run tests with `pnpm test`.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-opus-4-8@eu","usage":{"input":973,"output":315,"cacheRead":74025,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":75313,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784907632566,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-d4ee8df3-6994-4f60-87d2-e711b3941f3e","responseModel":"claude-opus-4-8"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01KMNJFRut4x6NRQMycoweQi","toolName":"subagent","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 21 tests remain green.\n\n### Step 5: Refactored APP Mass — `processClaim`\n\n```typescript\nconst processClaim = (policy: Policy, incident: Incident): ClaimResult => {\n  const uncappedPayout = incident.damages.reduce(\n    (sum, damage) => sum + damagePayout(damage), 0,           // reduce loop 5 + bindings + invocation ≈ 12\n  );\n  const payout = Math.floor(Math.min(uncappedPayout, policy.remainingCap)); // binding+2 invocations ≈ 6\n  policy.remainingCap -= payout;                              // assignment = 8\n  return { payout, remainingCap: policy.remainingCap };       // 2\n};\n```\n**Total Mass: ~28** — down from ~52.\n\nThe key win is eliminating three of the four `assignment` mutations (mass 6 each). The mutating `let payout` accumulator is replaced by a single immutable `reduce`, and the separate floor/clamp assignments collapse into one binding.\n\n## Refactoring Complete\n\n**Refactoring**: Simplified `processClaim`. Replaced the mutating `let payout` accumulator loop (which clamped cumulatively against the remaining cap on every iteration) with a declarative `reduce` computing the uncapped total, then a single `Math.floor(Math.min(...))` to apply the cap and MHPCO-favor rounding. This is mathematically equivalent because each per-damage payout is non-negative, so `min(sum, cap)` equals the cumulative clamp.\n\n- **Naming**: Evaluated first — `processClaim`, `damagePayout`, and `insuranceSumFor` already reveal intent; kept as-is. Introduced `uncappedPayout` as an explaining variable.\n- **Rule 2 (Reveals Intent)**: The two-step \"sum all payouts, then cap\" is now explicit rather than buried in a cumulative-clamp loop.\n- **Rule 4 (Fewest Elements)**: Removed the `let`, the loop body's intermediate `claimable`, and two reassignments.\n\n**Mass Change**: ~52 → ~28 (removed 3 of 4 assignments and the explicit loop).\n\n**Tests**: All 21 passing (20 todo untouched)."}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_15-24-24_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_opus-4-8-5/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 21\nRecent Green phase: Added claim processing. INSURANCE_VALUES map, Policy tracking (items + remainingCap = 2x insurance sum), processClaim computes payout per damage (amount - 100 deductible, floored, capped by remainingCap) and decrements remainingCap. runScenario now handles both quote and claim steps, storing policies by step index.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. Run tests with `pnpm test`.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 21\nRecent Green phase: Added claim processing. INSURANCE_VALUES map, Policy tracking (items + remainingCap = 2x insurance sum), processClaim computes payout per damage (amount - 100 deductible, floored, capped by remainingCap) and decrements remainingCap. runScenario now handles both quote and claim steps, storing policies by step index.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. Run tests with `pnpm test`.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784907637559},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I'll start by examining the current state of the implementation and tests."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01GSJWnammMG8tsmFvAk6pfN","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_15-24-24_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_opus-4-8-5/src/claim-office.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01DGPAXh4DdYL38pqPyuXaSr","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_15-24-24_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_opus-4-8-5/src/claim-office.spec.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-opus-4-8@eu","usage":{"input":282,"output":256,"cacheRead":9696,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":10234,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784907637579,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-a34a9c44-4acb-4e49-9159-ea450d41a1dc","responseModel":"claude-opus-4-8"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01GSJWnammMG8tsmFvAk6pfN","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"const PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_RATE = 0.1;\nconst CURSE_RATE = 0.5;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_RATE = 0.3;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD = 5;\nconst LOYALTY_RATE = 0.2;\nconst LOYALTY_THRESHOLD_YEARS = 2;\nconst FOLLOW_UP_RATE = 0.15;\nconst DEDUCTIBLE = 100;\nconst CAP_MULTIPLIER = 2;\n\nconst INSURANCE_VALUES: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 1000,\n  amulet: 600,\n  staff: 800,\n  potion: 400,\n  rune: 250,\n  moonstone: 250,\n};\n\ninterface Item {\n  type: string;\n  material?: string;\n  enchantment?: number;\n  cursed?: boolean;\n}\n\ninterface QuoteStep {\n  op: \"quote\";\n  items: Item[];\n}\n\ninterface Damage {\n  itemType: string;\n  amount: number;\n}\n\ninterface Incident {\n  cause: string;\n  damages: Damage[];\n}\n\ninterface ClaimStep {\n  op: \"claim\";\n  policy: number;\n  incident: Incident;\n}\n\ntype Step = QuoteStep | ClaimStep;\n\ninterface Scenario {\n  customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: number };\n  steps: Step[];\n}\n\ninterface QuoteResult {\n  premium: number;\n}\n\ninterface ClaimResult {\n  payout: number;\n  remainingCap: number;\n}\n\ntype StepResult = QuoteResult | ClaimResult;\n\nconst BASE_PREMIUMS: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n};\n\nconst COMPONENT_TYPES = new Set([\"rune\", \"moonstone\"]);\nconst COMPONENT_PREMIUM = 25;\nconst BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\nconst BLOCK_PREMIUM = 60;\n\nconst isComponent = (item: Item): boolean => COMPONENT_TYPES.has(item.type);\n\nconst componentGroupPremium = (count: number): number =>\n  count === BLOCK_SIZE ? BLOCK_PREMIUM : count * COMPONENT_PREMIUM;\n\nconst componentsBasePremium = (components: Item[]): number => {\n  const countsByType = new Map<string, number>();\n  for (const component of components) {\n    countsByType.set(component.type, (countsByType.get(component.type) ?? 0) + 1);\n  }\n  let total = 0;\n  for (const count of countsByType.values()) {\n    total += componentGroupPremium(count);\n  }\n  return total;\n};\n\nconst basePremiumFor = (item: Item): number => BASE_PREMIUMS[item.type];\n\nconst surchargeFor = (\n  mainItems: Item[],\n  qualifies: (item: Item) => boolean,\n  rate: number,\n): number =>\n  mainItems\n    .filter(qualifies)\n    .reduce((sum, item) => sum + basePremiumFor(item) * rate, 0);\n\nconst isCursed = (item: Item): boolean => item.cursed === true;\n\nconst isHighEnchantment = (item: Item): boolean =>\n  (item.enchantment ?? 0) >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD;\n\nconst percentageWhen = (base: number, rate: number, applies: boolean): number =>\n  applies ? base * rate : 0;\n\nconst isLoyalCustomer = (yearsWithMHPCO: number): boolean =>\n  yearsWithMHPCO >= LOYALTY_THRESHOLD_YEARS;\n\nconst quotePremium = (items: Item[], yearsWithMHPCO: number, isFollowUp: boolean): number => {\n  const mainItems = items.filter((item) => !isComponent(item));\n  const components = items.filter(isComponent);\n  const basePremium =\n    mainItems.reduce((sum, item) => sum + basePremiumFor(item), 0) +\n    componentsBasePremium(components);\n  const curseSurcharge = surchargeFor(mainItems, isCursed, CURSE_RATE);\n  const highEnchantmentSurcharge = surchargeFor(\n    mainItems,\n    isHighEnchantment,\n    HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_RATE,\n  );\n  const firstInsuranceSurcharge = basePremium * FIRST_INSURANCE_RATE;\n  const loyaltyDiscount = percentageWhen(basePremium, LOYALTY_RATE, isLoyalCustomer(yearsWithMHPCO));\n  const followUpDiscount = percentageWhen(basePremium, FOLLOW_UP_RATE, isFollowUp);\n  return Math.ceil(\n    basePremium +\n      curseSurcharge +\n      highEnchantmentSurcharge +\n      firstInsuranceSurcharge -\n      loyaltyDiscount -\n      followUpDiscount +\n      PROCESSING_FEE,\n  );\n};\n\nconst insuranceValueFor = (item: Item): number => INSURANCE_VALUES[item.type];\n\nconst insuranceSumFor = (items: Item[]): number =>\n  items.reduce((sum, item) => sum + insuranceValueFor(item), 0);\n\ninterface Policy {\n  items: Item[];\n  remainingCap: number;\n}\n\nconst damagePayout = (damage: Damage): number =>\n  Math.max(0, damage.amount - DEDUCTIBLE);\n\nconst processClaim = (policy: Policy, incident: Incident): ClaimResult => {\n  let payout = 0;\n  for (const damage of incident.damages) {\n    const claimable = Math.min(damagePayout(damage), policy.remainingCap - payout);\n    payout += claimable;\n  }\n  payout = Math.floor(payout);\n  policy.remainingCap -= payout;\n  return { payout, remainingCap: policy.remainingCap };\n};\n\nexport const runScenario = (scenario: Scenario): { results: StepResult[] } => {\n  let quoteCount = 0;\n  const policies: Record<number, Policy> = {};\n  const results: StepResult[] = scenario.steps.map((step, index) => {\n    if (step.op === \"quote\") {\n      const isFollowUp = quoteCount > 0;\n      quoteCount += 1;\n      policies[index] = {\n        items: step.items,\n        remainingCap: insuranceSumFor(step.items) * CAP_MULTIPLIER,\n      };\n      return {\n        premium: quotePremium(step.items, scenario.customer.yearsWithMHPCO, isFollowUp),\n      };\n    }\n    return processClaim(policies[step.policy], step.incident);\n  });\n  return { results };\n};\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784907640719},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01DGPAXh4DdYL38pqPyuXaSr","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { runScenario } from \"./claim-office.js\";\n\ndescribe(\"Claim Office - quote base premiums\", () => {\n  // Edge case: empty item list\n  it(\"empty item list -> premium 5 G (only processing fee)\", () => {\n    const out = runScenario({ customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 }, steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [] }] });\n    expect(out.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 5 });\n  });\n\n  // Base premiums per item type (base + 5 G fee, newcomer 0 years => +10% first insurance)\n  it(\"single sword newcomer -> 100 base +10 first +5 fee = 115 G\", () => {\n    const out = runScenario({ customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 }, steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] }] });\n    expect(out.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 115 });\n  });\n  it(\"single amulet newcomer -> 60 base +6 first +5 fee = 71 G\", () => {\n    const out = runScenario({ customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 }, steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"amulet\" }] }] });\n    expect(out.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 71 });\n  });\n  it(\"single staff newcomer -> 80 base +8 first +5 fee = 93 G\", () => {\n    const out = runScenario({ customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 }, steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"staff\" }] }] });\n    expect(out.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 93 });\n  });\n  it(\"single potion newcomer -> 40 base +4 first +5 fee = 49 G\", () => {\n    const out = runScenario({ customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 }, steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"potion\" }] }] });\n    expect(out.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 49 });\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"Claim Office - component building blocks\", () => {\n  it(\"2 runes -> 50 G base premium\", () => {\n    const out = runScenario({ customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 }, steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }] }] });\n    // base 50 + 10% first (5) + 5 fee = 60\n    expect(out.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 60 });\n  });\n  it(\"3 runes -> 60 G base premium (block applies)\", () => {\n    const out = runScenario({ customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 }, steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }] }] });\n    // block base 60 + 10% first (6) + 5 fee = 71\n    expect(out.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 71 });\n  });\n  it(\"4 runes -> 100 G base premium (no block, requires exactly 3)\", () => {\n    const out = runScenario({ customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 }, steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }] }] });\n    // base 100 + 10 first + 5 fee = 115\n    expect(out.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 115 });\n  });\n  it(\"7 runes -> 175 G base premium\", () => {\n    const items = Array.from({ length: 7 }, () => ({ type: \"rune\" }));\n    const out = runScenario({ customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 }, steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items }] });\n    // base 175 + 17.5 first + 5 fee = 197.5 -> 198\n    expect(out.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 198 });\n  });\n  it(\"2 runes + 1 moonstone -> 75 G base premium (no block: different types)\", () => {\n    const out = runScenario({ customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 }, steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"moonstone\" }] }] });\n    // base 75 + 7.5 first + 5 fee = 87.5 -> 88\n    expect(out.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 88 });\n  });\n  it(\"3 runes + 3 moonstones -> 120 G base premium (two separate blocks)\", () => {\n    const out = runScenario({ customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 }, steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [\n      { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" },\n      { type: \"moonstone\" }, { type: \"moonstone\" }, { type: \"moonstone\" },\n    ] }] });\n    // base 120 + 12 first + 5 fee = 137\n    expect(out.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 137 });\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"Claim Office - premium modifiers\", () => {\n  it(\"cursed sword newcomer -> 165 G (100 +50 curse +10 first +5 fee)\", () => {\n    const out = runScenario({ customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 }, steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: true }] }] });\n    expect(out.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 165 });\n  });\n  it(\"high-enchantment sword ench 5 newcomer -> 100 +30 +10 +5 = 145 G\", () => {\n    const out = runScenario({ customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 }, steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 5, cursed: false }] }] });\n    expect(out.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 145 });\n  });\n  it(\"sword ench 4 not cursed newcomer -> no high-ench surcharge = 115 G\", () => {\n    const out = runScenario({ customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 }, steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 4, cursed: false }] }] });\n    expect(out.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 115 });\n  });\n  it(\"cursed high-enchantment sword ench 5 -> both surcharges apply\", () => {\n    const out = runScenario({ customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 }, steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 5, cursed: true }] }] });\n    // 100 + 50 curse + 30 high-ench + 10 first + 5 fee = 195\n    expect(out.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 195 });\n  });\n  it(\"long-standing customer (2 years) -> loyalty discount applies\", () => {\n    const out = runScenario({ customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 2 }, steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: false }] }] });\n    // 100 base - 20 loyalty + 10 first + 5 fee = 95\n    expect(out.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 95 });\n  });\n  it(\"first insurance surcharge 10% applies per item in a quote\", () => {\n    const out = runScenario({ customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 3 }, steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: false }] }] });\n    // 100 base - 20 loyalty + 10 first + 5 fee = 95 (first insurance still applies for long-standing)\n    expect(out.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 95 });\n  });\n  it(\"follow-up contract 15% discount on each contract after first\", () => {\n    const out = runScenario({ customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 }, steps: [\n      { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: false }] },\n      { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: false }] },\n    ] });\n    // first: 100 + 10 first + 5 fee = 115\n    // second: 100 + 10 first - 15 follow-up + 5 fee = 100\n    expect(out.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 115 });\n    expect(out.results[1]).toEqual({ premium: 100 });\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"Claim Office - modifier scope on multi-item policies\", () => {\n  it(\"cursed sword + plain amulet -> curse surcharge on cursed item only -> 210 G before fee\", () => {\n    const out = runScenario({ customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 }, steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [\n      { type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: true },\n      { type: \"amulet\", material: \"silver\", enchantment: 2, cursed: false },\n    ] }] });\n    // base 160 + 50 curse (on sword only) = 210 before modifiers; + 16 first + 5 fee = 231\n    expect(out.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 231 });\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"Claim Office - rounding\", () => {\n  it(\"premium yielding 197.5 G -> 198 G (rounded up, MHPCO favor)\", () => {\n    const items = Array.from({ length: 7 }, () => ({ type: \"rune\" }));\n    const out = runScenario({ customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 }, steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items }] });\n    // base 175 + 17.5 first + 5 fee = 197.5 -> rounded up 198\n    expect(out.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 198 });\n  });\n  it.todo(\"payout yielding 350.5 G -> 350 G (rounded down, MHPCO favor)\");\n});\n\ndescribe(\"Claim Office - claim processing basics\", () => {\n  it(\"regular sword steel ench 3 damage 500 -> payout 400 (500 - 100 deductible)\", () => {\n    const out = runScenario({ customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 }, steps: [\n      { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3, cursed: false }] },\n      { op: \"claim\", policy: 0, incident: { cause: \"fire\", damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 500 }] } },\n    ] });\n    expect(out.results[1]).toEqual({ payout: 400, remainingCap: 1600 });\n  });\n  it.todo(\"damage to a rune (value 250) damage 200 -> payout 100 (200 - 100)\");\n  it.todo(\"high-enchantment ench 8 sword damage 1000 -> payout 400 (50% then deductible)\");\n  it.todo(\"dragon-material sword ench 8 damage 1000 -> payout 400 (high-ench wins, then deductible)\");\n});\n\ndescribe(\"Claim Office - enchantment threshold vs dragon material\", () => {\n  it.todo(\"dragon sword ench 9 damage 1000 -> payout 400 (50% wins then deductible)\");\n  it.todo(\"dragon sword ench 5 damage 800 -> payout 700 (full then deductible)\");\n  it.todo(\"steel sword ench 9 damage 1000 -> payout 400 (50% then deductible)\");\n});\n\ndescribe(\"Claim Office - deductible per damage event\", () => {\n  it.todo(\"dragon attack damages sword 500 + amulet 300 -> payout 600 (deductible per item)\");\n});\n\ndescribe(\"Claim Office - multiple items of same type\", () => {\n  it.todo(\"policy covers two swords -> insurance sum 2000, cap 4000\");\n  it.todo(\"dragon attack damages both swords -> each entry separate deductible\");\n  it.todo(\"more damage entries of a type than covered -> claim rejected (non-zero exit)\");\n});\n\ndescribe(\"Claim Office - cap and insurance sum\", () => {\n  it.todo(\"sword + amulet -> insurance sum 1600, cap 3200\");\n  it.todo(\"cursed sword premium 165 -> cap 2000 (based on unmodified insurance value)\");\n  it.todo(\"sword + 3 runes block -> insurance sum 1750 (block affects premium only)\");\n  it.todo(\"sword cap 2000; two 1500 claims -> first 1400 remaining 600, second 600 remaining 0\");\n});\n\ndescribe(\"Claim Office - error handling\", () => {\n  it.todo(\"quote with unknown item type -> non-zero exit, error to stderr\");\n  it.todo(\"claim references item not in policy -> non-zero exit\");\n  it.todo(\"claim damage entry with negative amount -> non-zero exit\");\n});\n\ndescribe(\"Claim Office - integration examples\", () => {\n  it.todo(\"newcomer with cursed sword -> 165 G\");\n  it.todo(\"long-standing customer 3yr second quote, cursed sword ench 7 -> 160 G\");\n});\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784907640719},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Running the tests to verify everything passes.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"Let me run the tests to confirm the current state."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_0158rthzo2QG8gN5innxduy7","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_15-24-24_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_opus-4-8-5 && pnpm test 2>&1 | tail -20"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-opus-4-8@eu","usage":{"input":7115,"output":164,"cacheRead":9976,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":17255,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784907640721,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-0b31ec76-f545-4a59-99b0-1d0485d10c0d","responseModel":"claude-opus-4-8"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_0158rthzo2QG8gN5innxduy7","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n> tdd-experiment-run@ test /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_15-24-24_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_opus-4-8-5\n> vitest run\n\n\n RUN  v1.6.1 /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_15-24-24_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_opus-4-8-5\n\n ✓ src/claim-office.spec.ts  (41 tests | 20 skipped) 4ms\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  21 passed | 20 todo (41)\n   Start at  15:40:45\n   Duration  193ms (transform 38ms, setup 0ms, collect 38ms, tests 4ms, environment 0ms, prepare 52ms)\n\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784907645823},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"All the tests are passing, so now I'm looking at the code to see where I can refactor and improve it. I'm examining the `processClaim` function that was recently written, which calculates damage payouts by subtracting the deductible and then iterates through incidents to compute the total claim payout.\n\nLooking at the naming and structure, the variable names are clear enough — `damagePayout` computes individual damage amounts, `claimable` represents what can actually be claimed after applying the policy cap. But the function has heavy assignment mass with the accumulating `payout` variable being reassigned multiple times through the loop, flooring, and cap reduction. I'm considering whether using a reduce pattern would help clean this up, though the cap logic makes it tricky since each damage's claimable amount depends on what's already been paid out.\n\nActually, I realize the cumulative clamping approach is mathematically equivalent to just summing all damages and then applying the cap once at the end — both produce the same final payout. So I can refactor to calculate the raw total payout from all damages, then floor and cap it in one step.\n\nRefactoring with reduce...\n\nNow I need to think through the order of operations with floor and min. Since amounts could be fractional (like 350.5 rounding down to 350), I need to make sure flooring happens after capping to the remaining cap, not before.\n\nMy approach of flooring the minimum of the raw sum and cap gives the same result as the current code's cumulative clamping approach, since both effectively cap the total to the remaining cap before flooring. This is cleaner and more readable—it clearly shows: sum the payouts, cap it, floor it.\n\nNow I'm analyzing the assignment cost in the current processClaim function to see where I can reduce complexity. So the Math.floor call brings that to 10, then I'm subtracting the payout from the remaining cap and returning both values—that's 8 more. The loop itself costs 6 total. Adding it all up across the statements gives roughly 52 operations. Now I'm refactoring to use reduce instead, which consolidates the damage iteration into a single operation that accumulates the payout sum.\n\nThe new approach calculates the raw payout first with reduce, then applies the floor and min functions to cap it, subtracts from the policy, and returns the result. That brings the total down to 31 operations—a significant improvement. The code is clearer too, so I'll apply this refactoring and run the tests to make sure everything still works.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"All 21 tests pass. Now let me analyze the code, focusing on the recently added claim-processing logic.\n\n## Refactoring Analysis\n\n### Step 1: Naming Evaluation (FIRST PRIORITY)\n\n- `damagePayout(damage)` — computes the uncapped payout for one damage (amount minus deductible, floored at zero). Name reveals intent well.\n- `processClaim(policy, incident)` — computes total payout and updates the policy cap. Name is accurate.\n- Inside `processClaim`, the variable `claimable` and the manual accumulation loop are the weak spot. The intent (\"sum the per-damage payouts, then apply the remaining cap\") is obscured by cumulative clamping inside a mutating loop.\n\n**Decision:** Keep the function names — they already reveal intent. Focus refactoring on the body of `processClaim`.\n\n### Step 2: Current APP Mass — `processClaim`\n\n```typescript\nconst processClaim = (policy: Policy, incident: Incident): ClaimResult => {\n  let payout = 0;                                                      // binding+const+assignment = 8\n  for (const damage of incident.damages) {                            // loop 5 + binding 1 = 6\n    const claimable = Math.min(damagePayout(damage), policy.remainingCap - payout); // ~10\n    payout += claimable;                                              // assignment = 8\n  }\n  payout = Math.floor(payout);                                        // assignment = 10\n  policy.remainingCap -= payout;                                      // assignment = 8\n  return { payout, remainingCap: policy.remainingCap };               // 2\n};\n```\n**Total Mass: ~52** (four assignments dominate).\n\n### Step 3: Apply Simple Design Rules\n\n- **Rule 1 (Tests Pass):** ✅ all 21 green.\n- **Rule 2 (Reveals Intent):** The cumulative-clamp loop hides a simpler truth. Because every `damagePayout` is `≥ 0`, the cumulative `Math.min` clamping is mathematically equivalent to `min(sum of all payouts, remainingCap)`. Expressing it directly reveals intent.\n- **Rule 3 (No Duplication):** none significant.\n- **Rule 4 (Fewest Elements):** the loop + three intermediate assignments are more elements than needed.\n\nThe `min(sum, cap)` reformulation also preserves the future floor-rounding requirement (350.5 → 350), since flooring the clamped sum once is equivalent.\n\nLet me apply the refactoring:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01JEa2wuuHNJynCEdNPyf7Fo","name":"edit","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_15-24-24_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_opus-4-8-5/src/claim-office.ts","edits":[{"oldText":"const processClaim = (policy: Policy, incident: Incident): ClaimResult => {\n  let payout = 0;\n  for (const damage of incident.damages) {\n    const claimable = Math.min(damagePayout(damage), policy.remainingCap - payout);\n    payout += claimable;\n  }\n  payout = Math.floor(payout);\n  policy.remainingCap -= payout;\n  return { payout, remainingCap: policy.remainingCap };\n};","newText":"const processClaim = (policy: Policy, incident: Incident): ClaimResult => {\n  const uncappedPayout = incident.damages.reduce(\n    (sum, damage) => sum + damagePayout(damage),\n    0,\n  );\n  const payout = Math.floor(Math.min(uncappedPayout, policy.remainingCap));\n  policy.remainingCap -= payout;\n  return { payout, remainingCap: policy.remainingCap };\n};"}]}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-opus-4-8@eu","usage":{"input":7539,"output":3460,"cacheRead":9997,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":20996,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784907645823,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-d3f98d08-2b09-4f