t 6, invocation 2, binding 1, constant 1\nreturn matchedItem                          -> binding 1\n```\nTotal (approx): **42** — one function carrying two concerns.\n\n## Step 3: Apply Rules\n\n- **Rule 1 (Tests Pass):** All 39 green. ✔\n- **Rule 2 (Reveals Intent):** Violated — mixed concerns. This is the target.\n- **Rule 3 (No Duplication):** No duplication introduced by the fix.\n- **Rule 4 (Fewest Elements):** Adds one small function, justified by clarity (Rule 2 outranks Rule 4).\n\n## Step 4: Implement"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_018SUqm7R5jhfeRmybZhXucF","name":"edit","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_15-24-24_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_opus-4-8-5/src/claim-office.ts","edits":[{"oldText":"const matchDamageToInsuredItem = (damage: Damage, unmatchedItems: Item[]): Item => {\n  if (damage.amount < 0) {\n    throw new Error(`Damage amount cannot be negative: ${damage.amount}`);\n  }\n  const matchIndex = unmatchedItems.findIndex((item) => item.type === damage.itemType);","newText":"const validateDamage = (damage: Damage): void => {\n  if (damage.amount < 0) {\n    throw new Error(`Damage amount cannot be negative: ${damage.amount}`);\n  }\n};\n\nconst matchDamageToInsuredItem = (damage: Damage, unmatchedItems: Item[]): Item => {\n  const matchIndex = unmatchedItems.findIndex((item) => item.type === damage.itemType);"},{"oldText":"  return incident.damages.reduce(\n    (sum, damage) => sum + damagePayout(damage, matchDamageToInsuredItem(damage, unmatchedItems)),\n    0,\n  );","newText":"  return incident.damages.reduce((sum, damage) => {\n    validateDamage(damage);\n    return sum + damagePayout(damage, matchDamageToInsuredItem(damage, unmatchedItems));\n  }, 0);"}]}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-opus-4-8@eu","usage":{"input":3863,"output":1869,"cacheRead":9696,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":15428,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRea